And since you obviously missed it the last time I explained;
You DON'T HAVE TO CHANGE THE CODE!  The same exact command compiled on two
different computers will produce two different results.  On an 8 bit machine
it will produce numbers from -127 to 128.  On a 16 bit machine it will produce
numbers much much larger.  This is a difficult concept?  There is NO change!
Further the machine specific code (of which this is NOT an example) is INCLUDED
in the standard release.  If amiga do this, If Ms-Dos do this, If overblown
calculator do this... etc.  It's all included in the standardly distributed
SOURCE code.

Thus, please refrain from telling people not to discuss modified versions.
They AREN'T modified... the program just works differently depending on the
machine it is running on.

